.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt X509_GET0_NOTBEFORE 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm X509_get0_notBefore ,
.Nm X509_getm_notBefore ,
.Nm X509_get0_notAfter ,
.Nm X509_getm_notAfter ,
.Nm X509_set1_notBefore ,
.Nm X509_set1_notAfter ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_get0_notBefore ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_get0_notAfter ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_set1_notBefore ,
.Nm X509_ACERT_set1_notAfter ,
.Nm X509_CRL_get0_lastUpdate ,
.Nm X509_CRL_get0_nextUpdate ,
.Nm X509_CRL_set1_lastUpdate ,
.Nm X509_CRL_set1_nextUpdate
.Nd get or set certificate or CRL dates
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/x509.h
.Ft const ASN1_TIME *
.Fo X509_get0_notBefore
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_TIME *
.Fo X509_get0_notAfter
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_TIME *
.Fo X509_getm_notBefore
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft ASN1_TIME *
.Fo X509_getm_notAfter
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_set1_notBefore
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_TIME *tm"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_set1_notAfter
.Fa "X509 *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_TIME *tm"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_GENERALIZEDTIME *
.Fo X509_ACERT_get0_notBefore
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_GENERALIZEDTIME *
.Fo X509_ACERT_get0_notAfter
.Fa "const X509 *x"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_set1_notBefore
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_GENERALIZEDTIME *tm"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_ACERT_set1_notAfter
.Fa "X509_ACERT *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_GENERALIZEDTIME *tm"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_TIME *
.Fo X509_CRL_get0_lastUpdate
.Fa "const X509_CRL *crl"
.Fc
.Ft const ASN1_TIME *
.Fo X509_CRL_get0_nextUpdate
.Fa "const X509_CRL *crl"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_CRL_set1_lastUpdate
.Fa "X509_CRL *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_TIME *tm"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo X509_CRL_set1_nextUpdate
.Fa "X509_CRL *x"
.Fa "const ASN1_TIME *tm"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn X509_get0_notBefore
and
.Fn X509_get0_notAfter
return the
.Sy notBefore
and
.Sy notAfter
fields of certificate
.Fa x
respectively.
The value returned is an internal pointer which must not be freed up
after the call.
.Fa x
.Sy MUST NOT
be NULL.
.Pp
.Fn X509_getm_notBefore
and
.Fn X509_getm_notAfter
are similar to
.Fn X509_get0_notBefore
and
.Fn X509_get0_notAfter
except they return non-constant mutable references to the associated
date field of the certificate.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set1_notBefore
and
.Fn X509_set1_notAfter
set the
.Sy notBefore
and
.Sy notAfter
fields of
.Fa x
to
.Fa tm .
Ownership of the passed parameter
.Fa tm
is not transferred by these functions so it must be freed up after the
call.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_notBefore
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_get0_notAfter
return the
.Sy notBefore
and
.Sy notAfter
fields of certificate
.Fa x
respectively.
returned is an internal pointer which must not be freed up after the
call.
.Pp
.Fn X509_ACERT_set1_notBefore
and
.Fn X509_ACERT_set1_notAfter
set the
.Sy notBefore
and
.Sy notAfter
fields of
.Fa x
to
.Fa tm .
Ownership of the passed parameter
.Fa tm
is not transferred by these functions so it must be freed up after the
call.
.Pp
.Fn X509_CRL_get0_lastUpdate
and
.Fn X509_CRL_get0_nextUpdate
return the
.Sy lastUpdate
and
.Sy nextUpdate
fields of
.Fa crl .
The value returned is an internal pointer which must not be freed up
after the call.
If the
.Sy nextUpdate
field is absent from
.Fa crl
then NULL is returned.
.Pp
.Fn X509_CRL_set1_lastUpdate
and
.Fn X509_CRL_set1_nextUpdate
set the
.Sy lastUpdate
and
.Sy nextUpdate
fields of
.Fa crl
to
.Fa tm .
Ownership of the passed parameter
.Fa tm
is not transferred by these functions so it must be freed up after the
call.
For
.Fn X509_CRL_set1_nextUpdate
the
.Fa tm
argument may be NULL, which implies removal of the optional
.Sy nextUpdate
field.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn X509_get0_notBefore ,
.Fn X509_get0_notAfter
and
.Fn X509_CRL_get0_lastUpdate
return a pointer to an
.Vt ASN1_TIME
structure.
.Pp
.Fn X509_CRL_get0_lastUpdate
return a pointer to an
.Vt ASN1_TIME
structure or NULL if the
.Sy lastUpdate
field is absent.
.Pp
.Fn X509_set1_notBefore ,
.Fn X509_set1_notAfter ,
.Fn X509_CRL_set1_lastUpdate
and
.Fn X509_CRL_set1_nextUpdate
return 1 for success or 0 for failure.
.Sh NOTES
Unlike the
.Vt X509
and
.Vt X509_CRL
routines, the
.Vt X509_ACERT
routines use the ASN1_GENERALIZEDTIME format instead of ASN1_TIME for
holding time data.
